       It is easy to see that Mohar’s Minty-type theorem follows from Theorems 1 and
2 immediately. Our approach here provides a new insight into the circular chromatic
numbers. It connects several different research fields, timed Petri nets [18], marked
graphs [8], scheduling, and coloring. It reveals that there are strong coherent and
coordinated relationships between these topics. We feel sure that the results in this
paper can shed insight on these areas.
